# Files Vercel must not receive.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE ADDING A DIRECTORY. Vercel applies this file to BOTH the CLI
# upload and the GitHub-integration build — the build log says "Removed N
# ignored files defined in .vercelignore" before it runs `vercel build`. An
# earlier version of this file listed scripts/ and design/, which deleted the
# build script and its source page and left the build with nothing to do.
#
# So this file may only exclude things the build does not need. The build
# (scripts/build-static-preview.sh, set as buildCommand in vercel.json) reads:
#
#     design/preview.html          the page itself
#     scripts/check-no-secrets.pl  the guard that stops a key being published
#
# Neither may be listed here, ever.
#
# It is NOT this file's job to stop application source being served publicly.
# `outputDirectory` in vercel.json does that: only dist/preview-site is served,
# whatever else exists in the source tree. Excluding the rest below is purely to
# keep the upload small.
#
# What this file IS for: the CLI case. `npx vercel` in the repo root uploads the
# working directory and does not read .gitignore, so it would publish the root
# preview.html (which holds the front-end dev's live Groq key) and .env. Both
# are gitignored, so every other guard here is blind to them — the secrets
# scanner skips them by design, the pre-commit hook scans the git index, and CI
# scans a git checkout. None of that protects an upload that never touches git.
#
# A key published this way is public the moment it uploads, and must be rotated
# rather than deleted.

# --- Live keys. The reason this file exists. Never remove these. ---
.env
.env.*
preview.html
preview*.html
*.key
*.pem

# --- Not needed by the build; excluded to keep the upload small. ---
# (Serving scope is enforced by outputDirectory, not by these lines.)
wp-content/
php/
tools/
docs/
.github/
.githooks/
*.zip

# --- Noise ---
node_modules/
vendor/
*.log
